---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { companyInfo } from '../lib/catalog';
const r = companyInfo.retail;
---
<BaseLayout title="Shipping & Returns | Tripadi International" description="Delivery times, charges and the returns policy for retail orders from Tripadi International.">
  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container-prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Retail orders</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.025em] text-ink-900 md:text-5xl">Shipping & returns</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="container-prose prose-editorial mt-10">
      <h2>Delivery within India</h2>
      <p>
        Orders are dispatched from our factory in Moradabad, Uttar Pradesh. In-stock pieces leave
        within two working days; a piece being made to your chosen finish takes longer and we will
        tell you the date before you pay.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Delivery is <strong>free on orders above ₹{r.free_shipping_above_inr.toLocaleString('en-IN')}</strong>.</li>
        <li>Below that, a flat charge of ₹{r.shipping_flat_inr.toLocaleString('en-IN')} applies.</li>
        <li>Metro and major cities: typically 3–5 working days from dispatch. Elsewhere: 5–8.</li>
        <li>A tracking reference is emailed the day your order leaves.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>International orders</h2>
      <p>
        We ship worldwide, but international orders are handled as a trade enquiry rather than through
        this checkout, because freight, duty and documentation have to be quoted for your destination.
        Write to us at <a href={`mailto:${companyInfo.sales_email}`}>{companyInfo.sales_email}</a> or use
        the <a href="/wholesale">enquiry form</a> and we will quote door-to-door.
      </p>

      <h2>Packing</h2>
      <p>
        Every piece is wrapped individually and packed in an export-grade carton. Anything plated or
        lacquered is interleaved so pieces never touch in transit. If a carton arrives visibly
        damaged, photograph it before opening — that photograph is what settles a claim.
      </p>

      <h2>Returns</h2>
      <p>
        You may return an unused piece in its original packing within <strong>{r.returns_days} days</strong> of
        delivery for a refund of the item price. Tell us first, by email or WhatsApp, so we can issue
        a return reference.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Return shipping is at your cost unless the piece is faulty or we sent the wrong item.</li>
        <li>Refunds are made to the original payment method within 7 working days of the piece reaching us.</li>
        <li>Bespoke pieces, custom finishes and anything carrying your logo cannot be returned — they cannot be resold. We will always send a sample before a custom order for exactly this reason.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Faults and damage</h2>
      <p>
        If a piece arrives damaged or develops a manufacturing fault, tell us within 30 days with
        photographs and we will repair, replace or refund it — our choice of remedy, your choice of
        which you would prefer, and in practice those are usually the same thing. Wear from normal
        service, tarnish on a lacquered piece that has been scoured or dishwashed, and damage from
        misuse are not manufacturing faults.
      </p>

      <h2>Trade orders</h2>
      <p>
        Wholesale and export orders are governed by the terms on the proforma invoice, not by this
        page. See <a href="/export">export and shipping</a> for Incoterms, packing and documentation.
      </p>

      <h2>Talk to us</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${companyInfo.email}`}>{companyInfo.email}</a> · {companyInfo.phone} · {companyInfo.hours}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
